{"key":"3ce06645e20754cd","source_file":"Potts Ph - Po.json","source_id":17025,"source_url":"concordance-pluto-ppl-pluto","term":"Pluto","headwords":["Pluto"],"latin":["Pluto"],"header_pairs":[{"english":["Pluto"],"latin":["Pluto"]}],"header_sentences":[],"redirect_xref":null,"works":["AR","DP","SE","TCR"],"contexts":[{"reference":{"work":"DP","section":"139","subsection":"8"},"text":"Worshipped like Plutos in Hell.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AR","section":"752","subsection":"2"},"text":"They are thus like the infernal gods, whom the ancients called Plutos.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AR","section":"792","subsection":"end"},"text":"No wonder that... they are carried away... to sacrifices to demons called Plutos.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"TCR","section":"159","subsection":"5"},"text":"See Apollo.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"TCR","section":"178","subsection":null},"text":"It would follow... that there is a god in the centre of the earth, who... may be called Pluto.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"TCR","section":"404","subsection":"end"},"text":"These were called by the Ancients, Mammons, and by the Greeks, Plutos.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"SE","section":"4427","subsection":null},"text":"Concerning a Pluto.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"SE","section":"4428","subsection":null},"text":"One who said he was Pluto; being one of those called Plutonics, who have the phantasy of seeing immense treasures of gold. Described.","comment":null,"footnote":null}],"slug":"pluto","url":"/meta/potts/pluto/"}